  "id": "USN-9132-1",
  "summary": "apng2gif vulnerabilities",
  "details": "Dileep Kumar Jallepalli discovered that apng2gif incorrectly handled\nloading APNG files, leading to an integer overflow and a heap-based buffer\nover-read. If a user or automated system were tricked into converting a\nspecially crafted APNG file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to\nobtain sensitive information or cause a denial of service. (CVE-2017-6960)\n\nDileep Kumar Jallepalli discovered that apng2gif did not limit the size of\nmemory allocations when reading APNG chunks. If a user or automated  system\nwere tricked into converting a specially crafted APNG file, an  attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause apng2gif to crash, resulting  in a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2017-6961)\n\nDileep Kumar Jallepalli discovered that apng2gif incorrectly handled\ncertain  chunk sizes, leading to an integer overflow and a heap-based\nbuffer overflow.  If a user or automated system were tricked into\nconverting a specially crafted  APNG file, an attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause apng2gif to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\npossibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2017-6962)",
